> Hear that? A twinkling star just tinkled to the ground!
> — Ciaccona

 She is a free-spirited, romantic, sincere, and whimsical bard wandering [[Rinascita]] in search of inspiration. A passionate musician, poet, and storyteller for both commoners as well as the Divinity, Ciaccona aims to spread her talents, truths, and discoveries of the world around her to all those daring enough to listen.

==Official Introduction==
> Ciaccona, the bard of Rinascita, is free-spirited, romantic, sincere, and passionate.

On her journey, she sang radiant poems of saints and heroes, weaving tales of people, miracles, turmoil, and suffering—along with the sorrow of death and farewell.
> — Introduction from the [https://wutheringwaves.kurogames.com/en/main#resonators Official Website.]

==Trivia==
===Etymology===
* A ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaconne chaconne]'' (''ciaccona'' in Italian) is a style of musical composition popular during the Baroque Era (1600-1750 A.D.).
* ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toccata Toccata]'' (from Italian ''toccare'', literally, "to touch", with "toccata" being the action of touching) is a virtuoso piece of music typically for a keyboard or plucked string instrument featuring fast-moving, lightly fingered or otherwise virtuosic passages or sections, generally emphasizing the dexterity of the performer's fingers.